This code shows that Int64 fields intentionally use json.Number(dataString).Int64() to parse input values. The json.Number type in Go accepts both numeric JSON values AND string-encoded numeric values, then converts them to int64. This is a deliberate type coercion feature, not a bug. When given the string "100", json.Number successfully parses and converts it to the integer 100.
